A['H264ENCSCENECUT']=('SR680 (LEDGER.md)','Sheets: handlers.md (§5 H264ENC-RC row L106 in place; BP-handlers-4, -14 KEPT). CHARTER: Stria (CODEX §2 A/V), seam shared-core (h264enc_core, no_std, the one encoder both faces link) + host handler (stria nle_export.rs one option line) + tools/nle.',
"""The H.264 encoder codes an IDR every `gop` frames and nowhere else (h264enc_core lib.rs :595 `idr = frames % gop == 0`; the B-frame group rule :603-:621), so a hard cut inside a GOP is coded as a P / B picture predicting across it (the worst case for the rate model and for seeking). H264ENC-RC (SR218) owes scene-cut detection: an IDR on a complexity jump. GOAL: `Config::scenecut`, off by default (every pinned byte unchanged), an IDR at a detected cut, exposed by `nle export --scenecut`.
M1 measure: `encode` (:590) and `next_pic` / `group` (:603-:621: how a B group closes and what an IDR resets — frame_num, POC, the DPB), rc.rs's per-row SAD complexity (what inter / intra SADs the motion search and the intra decision already compute per MB and where they are summed; the Rc's complexity term), the pinned-bytes tests (tests/*.rs: which pin whole streams), `H264Encoder` in handlers/stria/src/nle_export.rs (the Config builder) and tools/nle's flags (src/main.rs), the x264 scene-cut rule as published (icost / pcost with a bias: cite it; implement the cheap form the encoder's own numbers allow).
M2 build: `Config::scenecut: Option<u8>` (None = off; Some(k) = the threshold in percent, 40 the documented default): before a picture is coded as P (or as a B group's first P), the detector compares the picture's inter cost (the motion search's summed best SAD against its reference) with its intra cost (the intra mode decision's summed SAD; if the intra cost is only known after the mode decision, run the decision for the detector once — say what it costs) and codes an IDR when inter > (1 - k/100) x intra, restarting the GOP count exactly as a scheduled IDR does (the same `code(Pic::Idr, ..)` path; no second IDR form); a `min_keyint` guard = gop / 4 (no cut IDR within it of the last IDR unless inter > intra outright); in B-frame mode a cut closes the open group at the cut (the measured group rule) and the cut picture is the IDR. Stria: `H264Encoder::with_scenecut(k)` -> the Config field, `nle export --scenecut [k]` (tools/nle: one flag; nle_export.rs: ONE option line), the JSON line gaining `"scenecut":k` only if a reader exists.
M3 tests (tests/scenecut.rs new, or rc.rs tail): a synthetic stream of flat / gradient frames with a hard cut (pattern A for 10 frames, then pattern B) at gop 30: with scenecut Some(40) the frame at the cut is an IDR (read the access unit's NAL types through the crate's own reader / the existing test helpers) and the next scheduled IDR moves accordingly; with None the stream's bytes equal the pinned ones (every existing pinned test unchanged); the min_keyint guard (a second cut 3 frames later stays a P); B-frame mode: the group closes at the cut.""",
'H264ENC-TWOPASS, H264ENC-ACTIVITY (per-MB activity masking), H264ENC-HRD (VUI nal_hrd_parameters, filler), H264ENC-SCENECUT-FADE (a fade is not a cut: the gradual rule).',
'unaos/libs/media/h264enc_core/src/lib.rs (the Config field as the LAST field; the IDR decision in `encode` / `next_pic` IN PLACE, one line each; the detector fn at the FILE TAIL under a named block comment), unaos/libs/media/h264enc_core/src/rc.rs (only if the costs live there: in place), unaos/libs/media/h264enc_core/tests/scenecut.rs (new) or tests/rc.rs (tail), handlers/stria/src/nle_export.rs (ONE option line in place), tools/nle/src/main.rs (the flag, in place), docs/dev/blueprint/handlers.md (§5 row L106 IN PLACE: `Owed: a two-pass mode; scene-cut detection (...)` -> `scene-cut detection BUILT by SR680 (...)`), docs/dev/LEDGER.md (SR680 at the END). No other arc touches these files.',
exc('media','`cargo test -p h264enc_core` then `cargo build -p nle`'))
A['AETHERIMGALT']=('SR681 (LEDGER.md)','Sheets: handlers.md (§5 AETHERMAC-RUN row L90: the `AETHER-IMG-ALT (a host img that fails paints no alt text)` clause and its `AETHER-IMG-ALT carried` mention, in place; BP-handlers-1..14 KEPT), bar.md (read). CHARTER: Aether (CODEX §2 Web, Amendment II), seam shared-core (layout_core) + host handler (handlers/aether render).',
"""An `<img>` whose image is unavailable (the fetch failed, a bad URL, an unsupported format, no src) paints NOTHING on the host: layout_core's img rule (tree.rs :1937) sizes it from width / height attributes else the intrinsic size, and the render img arm (handlers/aether/src/render/mod.rs :2864) paints the bitmap or nothing (`image_painted` false). Chromium (HTMLImageFallbackHelper + html.css) renders the ALT TEXT: with no dimensions, an img with non-empty alt lays out as inline text in the element's font (no box, no border); with dimensions (or CSS size) it is a box of that size with a 1px solid silver (#c0c0c0) inset border, the broken-image icon at the top-left and the alt text beside / under it, clipped; an EMPTY alt paints nothing (and takes no space when unsized). GOAL: the host paints Chromium's alt rendering; AETHER.ELF is owed.
M1 measure: tree.rs :1937 (the img arm of the sizing rule: what `img_intrinsic` returns when the host has no image; where the host's image table says 'failed' vs 'pending' — read the images module and the fetch pass in handlers/aether/src/net/mod.rs / images/: an image still loading must NOT flash alt text (Chromium shows nothing until the load fails), so the rule needs the tri-state), `image_alt_label` (:891) and `is_image_input` (:884, SR461's rule for input image's alt), render/mod.rs :2864-:2870 (`image_painted`) and `caption_box`, the font / colour the element's text would take, Chromium's exact rule from HTMLImageFallbackHelper.cpp and html.css (cite lines).
M2 build: layout_core: ONE `img_fallback(node, image_state) -> ImgFallback { None, InlineAlt(text), BoxedAlt(text) }` at tree.rs's tail: a FAILED image with non-empty alt and no author / attribute size = InlineAlt (the img box becomes an inline text run of the alt, measured through the same text extents the control labels use; the sizing rule's img arm takes it IN PLACE: one line), with a size = BoxedAlt (the box keeps its size); a pending image or an empty alt = None (today's behaviour). Host render img arm: BoxedAlt paints the 1px solid #c0c0c0 inset border over the box and the alt text at (x + 1 + 16 + 2?, the top): use Chromium's offsets as measured, in the element's font and colour, clipped to the box; InlineAlt paints as the text run it laid out as (the inline path should already paint it if the layout made it a text run: measure, and if the render needs an arm, ONE arm); no icon bitmap (owe AETHER-IMG-BROKENICON: the tree has no icon asset).
M3 tests (handlers/aether/src/engine_tests.rs tail): `img_alt_inline_when_unsized_and_failed` (the box width = the alt text's extents, the text painted), `img_alt_boxed_when_sized` (the 200x100 box, the border pixels, the text inside), `img_empty_alt_paints_nothing`, `img_pending_paints_nothing_yet`; layout_core tests if the rule has a std-free seam.""",
'AETHER-IMG-ALT-ELF (AETHER.ELF\'s img path), AETHER-IMG-BROKENICON (the 16x16 broken-image icon: an asset), AETHER-IMG-ALT-INLINE-WRAP (a long alt wrapping like text), AETHER-IMAGEINPUT-FACE carried.',
'unaos/libs/web/layout_core/src/tree.rs (the img arm of the sizing rule IN PLACE at :1937, one line; `img_fallback` at the FILE TAIL under a named block comment), handlers/aether/src/render/mod.rs (the img arm IN PLACE at :2864-:2870; a tail paint fn), handlers/aether/src/engine_tests.rs (tail), docs/dev/blueprint/handlers.md (§5 row L90 IN PLACE: `AETHER-IMG-ALT (...)` -> `AETHER-IMG-ALT BUILT by SR681 (...)`), docs/dev/LEDGER.md (SR681 at the END). Shared with AETHERFILECHOSEN on tree.rs (it edits `file_labels` :897 and adds a tail fn), render/mod.rs (it edits `paint_file_color` :1449) and engine_tests.rs (tails): different arms, name your hunks.',
exc('aether','`cargo test -p layout_core` then `cargo test -p aether --lib -- img_alt img_empty img_pending`'))
A['AETHERFILECHOSEN']=('SR682 (LEDGER.md)','Sheets: handlers.md (§5 AETHERMAC-RUN row L90: the `AETHER-FILECHOSEN (no picker: the status is always No file chosen)` clause in place; BP-handlers-1..14 KEPT), bar.md (read). CHARTER: Aether (CODEX §2 Web), seam shared-core (layout_core) + host handler (render) + AETHER.ELF (user-aether paint).',
"""An `<input type=file>` shows Chromium's two parts: the Choose File(s) button (SR456 / SR459 / SR463 built its edges, face and caption) and the STATUS text after it — `No file chosen`, or the chosen file's name (its basename; `multiple` with N > 1 files: `N files`) — in the control's font, start-aligned 4 px after the button (Blink LayoutFileUploadControl: kAfterButtonSpacing = 4; kDefaultWidthNumChars = 34), clipped to the box with an ellipsis. layout_core's `file_labels` (tree.rs :897) returns the two literal strings and `control_intrinsic`'s file arm (:783) sizes the status at the literal; the host paints only the caption (render/mod.rs `paint_file_color` :1449) and the ELF the same (user-aether paint.rs `file_color` :528), so the status is never painted and a chosen file never shows. GOAL: the status text, from the value, painted on the host and the ELF.
M1 measure: `file_labels` and its two readers; `control_intrinsic`'s file arm (the status width term: the literal's width vs the value's); `paint_file_color`'s layout of the button sub-box (SR459: at the content origin with `push_button_edges`); `file_color` in the ELF; how a file input's value is held on the host (`forms/`: the `value` attribute; is there a picker that sets it? the sheet says none: the value attribute (`C:\\fakepath\\name.ext` or a plain name) is the source, tests set it); the element's font / colour at paint; Chromium's status rules (LayoutFileUploadControl.cpp: `FileChooser`'s displayed name, the ellipsis side (start, with `…`), the colour (the element's), the `multiple` count string from the locale: use `N files`).
M2 build: layout_core: ONE `file_status(value: Option<&str>, multiple: bool, count: usize) -> Cow<str>` at tree.rs's tail (empty value -> `No file chosen`; one file -> the basename after the last `\\` or `/`; N > 1 -> `N files`), `file_labels`'s status read through it (in place, one line) so `control_intrinsic` sizes the box from the real status; host `paint_file_color`'s file arm paints the status 4 px after the button's right edge, vertically centred like the caption, in the element's font and colour, clipped to the box's content right edge with a trailing `…` (ONE ellipsis helper if the render has none: measure `caption_box` and the text clip the control arm uses); ELF `file_color` paints the same through its txt path (code-only; the seat's build-std check compiles it).
M3 tests (engine_tests.rs tail): `file_status_no_file_chosen_painted` (value absent: the text's pixels at x = button right + 4), `file_status_shows_basename` (value `C:\\fakepath\\report.pdf` -> `report.pdf`), `file_status_multiple_counts` (two names -> `2 files`: decide how a multi-value is carried — the value attribute's first name only, Chromium shows `N files` from the FileList; with no picker use a test-only `files` count on the element if one exists, else document the single-name rule and omit this test), `file_status_ellipsized` (a 60-char name in a 227 px box ends with `…` inside the box); layout_core tests/button_label.rs tail: `file_status_width_follows_the_value`.""",
'AETHER-FILEPICKER (a picker through quartzite\'s open dialog: the value set from the chosen path), AETHER-FILECHOSEN-ELF-ELLIPSIS (the ELF txt path\'s ellipsis if it has none), AETHER-FILE-DRAGDROP.',
'unaos/libs/web/layout_core/src/tree.rs (`file_labels` :897 IN PLACE one line; `file_status` at the FILE TAIL under a named block comment; `control_intrinsic`\'s file arm in place only if the width term must read the value), handlers/aether/src/render/mod.rs (`paint_file_color` :1449 in place; a tail helper), unaos/crates/user-aether/src/paint.rs (`file_color` :528 in place), handlers/aether/src/engine_tests.rs (tail), unaos/libs/web/layout_core/tests/button_label.rs (tail), docs/dev/blueprint/handlers.md (§5 row L90 IN PLACE: `AETHER-FILECHOSEN (...)` -> `AETHER-FILECHOSEN BUILT by SR682 (...)`), docs/dev/LEDGER.md (SR682 at the END). Shared with AETHERIMGALT on tree.rs / render/mod.rs / engine_tests.rs and with AETHERIMAGEINPUTELF on paint.rs (it edits the img path; you edit file_color): name your hunks.',
exc('aether','`cargo test -p layout_core` then `cargo test -p aether --lib -- file_status`'))
A['AETHERIMAGEINPUTELF']=('SR683 (LEDGER.md)','Sheets: handlers.md (§5 AETHERMAC-RUN row L90: `AETHER-IMAGEINPUT-ELF (AETHER.ELF has no image path)` in place; BP-handlers-1..14 KEPT; the ELF lays out through layout_core::layout (SR463)). CHARTER: Aether (CODEX §2 Web), seam the ring-3 face (unaos/crates/user-aether, no_std / no_main) over the shared core (layout_core).',
"""AETHERIMAGEINPUTFETCH (SR461) made the HOST fetch, size and paint an `<input type=image src=...>` like an img through ONE layout_core predicate `is_image_input` (tree.rs :884) and the img sizing rule (:1937); AETHER.ELF (unaos/crates/user-aether) never fetches it: its image collection and paint path (paint.rs: the `ImgHost` img path; net.rs `fetch` :337) know `<img>` only, so on UnaOS an image input paints its alt label at best. GOAL: the ELF fetches and paints an image input through its existing img path; the alt label (layout_core `image_alt_label` :891, the rule the host uses) when there is no image.
M1 measure: the ELF's image collection (where it walks the DOM for `img` src: paint.rs / style.rs / main.rs — grep `"img"` and `src`), its fetch (net.rs :337 `fetch`, the content-type read :407, the decode through pixel_core?), its paint of a bitmap into a box (the fn and how it reads the laid-out box), `caption` (:483, the button alt label SR434 / SR457 built) and how `file_color` (:528) paints a sub-box, layout_core's `is_image_input` / `image_alt_label` / the img sizing rule as the ELF already runs them (the ELF links layout_core: confirm in its Cargo.toml and the `layout` call), SR461's host rule (handlers/aether/src/render/mod.rs :2864 the arm, net/mod.rs `collect_image_urls`) as the behaviour to match.
M2 build: the ELF's image collection admits an element where `layout_core::is_image_input` holds (ONE predicate, no tag test of its own) and fetches its `src` through the same fetch and decode; the paint arm that blits an img's bitmap takes the same element (the laid-out box is already the image's size by layout_core's rule); with no bitmap (a failed fetch, no src) the alt label (`image_alt_label(alt, value)`) is painted centred through `caption`'s path (the SR434 rule), no ButtonFace fill (SR455 / AETHER-IMAGEINPUT-FACE: say whether the ELF's face fill (`BUTTON_FACE`, SR463) touches an image input today, and exclude it through `is_image_input` if it does, one line); the value text is never painted over a bitmap (SR461's `image_painted` rule). Every edit in paint.rs / net.rs in place or at the file tail under a named block comment.
M3 proof (no host test harness runs the ELF): the two build-std checks of hosttests.sh, from your worktree root with YOUR worktree's target spec paths: `cargo check --release -Z json-target-spec --manifest-path unaos/crates/user-aether/Cargo.toml -Z build-std=core,compiler_builtins,alloc -Z build-std-features=compiler-builtins-mem --target /home/user/exec/aetherimageinputelf/unaos/x86_64-unknown-none.json` and the same with `aarch64-base.json`, each rc=0 (quote the Finished line); plus, if user-aether has any host-run unit test or KAT binary (measure), it. The seat compiles the fold the same way.""",
'AETHER-IMAGEINPUT-FACE (the ButtonFace guard on the host), AETHER-IMG-ALT-ELF (a plain img\'s alt text in the ELF: the same caption path, the IMGALT arc\'s host rule once folded), AETHER-ELFCONTROLFRAME.',
'unaos/crates/user-aether/src/paint.rs (the img paint arm and the alt caption IN PLACE; a tail fn under a named block comment), unaos/crates/user-aether/src/net.rs or the file holding the image collection (in place, one line: the predicate), unaos/crates/user-aether/src/style.rs only if the collection lives there, docs/dev/blueprint/handlers.md (§5 row L90 IN PLACE: `AETHER-IMAGEINPUT-ELF (...)` -> `AETHER-IMAGEINPUT-ELF BUILT by SR683 (...)`), docs/dev/LEDGER.md (SR683 at the END). Shared with AETHERFILECHOSEN on paint.rs (it edits `file_color` :528; you edit the img arm): name your hunks. No host crate file.',
exc('ua','the two `cargo check --release -Z json-target-spec ... -Z build-std=core,compiler_builtins,alloc -Z build-std-features=compiler-builtins-mem --target <your worktree>/unaos/{x86_64-unknown-none,aarch64-base}.json` lines above (the toolchain from the toml pin; no `+nightly`)'))
A['AETHERFONTDBCACHE']=('SR684 (LEDGER.md)','Sheets: handlers.md (§5 AETHERMAC-RUN row L90: `owed AETHER-FONTDB-CACHE (a persisted index under UnaPaths)` and the later `AETHER-FONTDB-CACHE ... stay owed` mention, in place; BP-handlers-1..14 KEPT). CHARTER: Aether (CODEX §2 Web) through its host font stack `libs/text_host` (QUARTZFONT SR64: shared by Aether and quartzite); the cache dir is the caller\'s (Aether\'s `storage::platform_data_dir`), text_host gains no aether dependency.',
"""text_host's `FontDb::discover` (libs/text_host/src/db.rs :269) indexes every installed face at EVERY process start by reading each file's table directory and six tables (AETHER-FONTDB-LAZY SR419: bounded reads, `[fonts] discover files= bytes_read= faces= ms=`), and `FontDb::covers` (SR425) reads cmaps lazily. The index is rebuilt on every launch though the font files have not changed. The row owes AETHER-FONTDB-CACHE: a persisted index. GOAL: the discovered index persisted under the caller's data dir and re-read when every file is unchanged; a miss or a stale entry re-discovers and rewrites.
M1 measure: `discover` and `faces_in_header` / `face_record` (what `FaceInfo` :58 holds: path, index, families, full_names, style — every field the cache must carry), `Config` (what dirs it scans, how the caller builds it: `handlers/aether/src/fonts/*.rs` and quartzite's caller — grep `FontDb::discover` / `Config {`), the process-wide db (:388 `OnceLock`), `fallback_order` and the cmap `OnceLock`s (lazy: unaffected by a cached index), `handlers/aether/src/storage/mod.rs:409 platform_data_dir` (the UnaPaths rule: what dir it yields per platform), the test fixtures text_host has (`fontdb_lazy_fixture_kat`: which font files it uses) and the KNOWN RED test.
M2 build: `Config.cache_dir: Option<PathBuf>` (None = no cache: today's path byte for byte; the ONE new field, last); `discover` with a cache dir reads `<cache_dir>/fontdb-index.v1` — a text index you define in ONE module (`db_cache.rs`, no serde, no new dep): a header line (format version, the scanned dir list), then per file one line `path \\t size \\t mtime_ns` followed by one line per face (index, families, full_names, style fields; tab-separated, `\\t` / `\\n` / `\\\\` escaped) — validates it against the live dir walk (every indexed file still present with the same size and mtime_ns, no file in the walk missing from the index) and on a HIT builds the FontDb from the records (bytes_read = 0), on a MISS (no index, unreadable, a version mismatch, a new file) or STALE (a changed or removed file) runs today's discovery and writes the index atomically (temp file in the same dir + rename), logging `[fonts] discover files= bytes_read= faces= ms= cache=hit|miss|stale|off` (the one existing line, one field appended). Aether's caller passes `platform_data_dir().join("fonts")` (one line); quartzite's caller passes None unless it already has a data dir (measure, say).
M3 tests (libs/text_host tests tail or db.rs's test module): with a tempdir under /root/unaos-bench/scratch/cloud/wave36/aetherfontdbcache/scratch/ holding copies of the fixture fonts: discover twice -> the second logs cache=hit and its `FaceInfo` list equals the first field for field; touch one file's mtime -> stale, re-discovered, equal list; copy a third font in -> miss; truncate the index -> miss; `cache_dir: None` -> off and the SR419 KATs unchanged. The KNOWN RED (`resolution_and_fallback_vs_fontconfig`) is pre-existing: name it, do not touch it.""",
'AETHER-FONTDB-CACHE-WATCH (a directory watch instead of the walk), AETHER-FONTDB-CACHE-CMAP (the covers() cmap results persisted too), AETHER-EMOJI, AETHER-CJK-GENERIC carried.',
'libs/text_host/src/db.rs (`Config`\'s last field; `discover` IN PLACE: the one read-or-build branch; the index read / write / validate in a NEW `libs/text_host/src/db_cache.rs` module), libs/text_host/src/lib.rs (the `mod` line), handlers/aether/src/fonts/<the Config builder> (one line), libs/text_host tests (tail), docs/dev/blueprint/handlers.md (§5 row L90 IN PLACE: `owed AETHER-FONTDB-CACHE (a persisted index under UnaPaths)` -> `AETHER-FONTDB-CACHE BUILT by SR684 (...)` and the `stay owed` mention adjusted), docs/dev/LEDGER.md (SR684 at the END). No other arc touches text_host.',
exc('aether','`cargo test -p text_host`'))

launch=open(f'{W}/launch-prompt.txt').read()
for n,v in A.items():
    lid,charter,goal,owed,files,ex=v; low=n.lower()
    arc=(f'ARC: {n} (wave36 cut70h). Ledger: {lid}. Branch exec-rmbp-{low}, worktree /home/user/exec/{low}, cut from {cut}. This is a HOST arc (your LEDGER row at the END of the table in docs/dev/LEDGER.md: 7 cells, no `|` inside a cell, status fixed-unflown, the test command and its counts in the last cell). {charter}\n'
         f'GOAL: {goal}\nOWED (inside your row, not built): {owed}\nFILES: {files}\n{seam}\n{ex}\n{codeonly}\n')
    open(f'{W}/{low}.md','w').write(arc); os.makedirs(f'{W}/{low}',exist_ok=True)
    lp=launch.replace('NAME',low).replace('2879aed46',cut)
    lp=lp.replace('CODE ONLY: no cargo check, no ./arroyo gates, no QEMU','CODE ONLY except the arc EXCEPTION line (the named host cargo command on the named shared target dir, nothing else)')
    lp=lp.replace('(it carries the MEASURED DESIGN from the first build, lost at a container reset — re-measure it against the code at your cut, every anchor may have moved)','(its anchors were read at the cut; re-measure each against the code)')
    open(f'{W}/{low}/launch.txt','w').write(lp); print(n,len(arc),len(lp))
